  "foaf:name": "Deep Ocean Microbial Symbionts",
  "sdo:name": "Deep Ocean Microbial Symbionts",
  "sdo:description": "The DOMS project will contribute to the DOME Programme by advancing our understanding of deep-ocean microbial symbionts, which are fundamental to the survival, adaptation, and ecological success of marine life in Earth&#x27;s largest and least explored biome. It will: (1) employ cutting-edge technologies to discover and characterize the taxonomic and functional diversity of microbial symbionts associated with diverse deep-sea fauna, aiming to uncover novel genes and adaptive strategies; (2) elucidate the ecological significance and biogeochemical roles of symbiotic interactions, focusing on nutrient cycling, host physiological contributions, and environmental factors on holobiont stability and functionality; (3) investigate the interplay within holobionts, including the roles of viruses in shaping symbiont communities and host health; and (4) ensure all generated data and knowledge are openly shared via the OceanMicrobe platform, supporting DOME&#x27;s commitment to the BBNJ Agreement.",
